(define-memory antigravity-login-is-operator-only
  "In opencodex, google-antigravity (Google Antigravity / Cloud Code Assist) OAuth can get the Google account's Gemini + Antigravity access DISABLED ('This service has been disabled in this account for violation of Terms of Service'), so every path to adding one demands the owner's own acknowledgement, and an AGENT MUST NEVER give it: AGENTS_INSTALL.md forbids passing --accept-antigravity-risk, answering the y/N prompt, sending acknowledgeAntigravityRisk:true to POST /api/oauth/login or /api/oauth/accounts/import, or ticking the dashboard checkbox. Verified on this box: that POST returns 403 {\"code\":\"antigravity_risk_not_acknowledged\"} - treat as final, relay the warning and let the operator click. What an agent MAY do: `ocx provider add google-antigravity` (no credential, no upstream contact) - but the running proxy only picks it up after `systemctl --user restart opencodex-proxy` (`--live` refuses because the target roster lacks the preset). Flow facts: redirect_uri http://127.0.0.1:51121/callback bound on the proxy machine, PKCE S256, access_type=offline, prompt=consent; from a remote browser the redirect fails locally, so paste the whole address-bar URL into the dialog's 'redirect URL or code' field (POST /api/oauth/login/code {provider,input} accepts a URL or a bare code), or ssh -L 51121. Safer supported alternative the docs name: the `google` preset with a Gemini API key."
  :type :reference)
